1
00:00:00,192 --> 00:00:06,013
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,019 --> 00:00:09,019
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,019 --> 00:00:10,019
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,019 --> 00:00:11,019
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:11,845 --> 00:00:14,215
[Episode 13]

6
00:00:14,901 --> 00:00:18,049
Even if it's difficult, make sure
you stretch at home every day.

7
00:00:18,049 --> 00:00:21,917
Take your medication twice a day,
and I'll see you again in a week.

8
00:00:21,917 --> 00:00:23,445
Yes, Doctor. Thank you.

9
00:00:23,445 --> 00:00:25,145
Take care.

10
00:00:28,479 --> 00:00:31,675
Dr. Oh, that was your last patient.

11
00:00:31,675 --> 00:00:33,435
You worked hard today.

12
00:00:33,435 --> 00:00:36,255
Goodness, I didn't realize it was this late.

13
00:00:36,255 --> 00:00:38,556
You did a great job too, Ms. Jung.

14
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,407
Jeez.

15
00:00:50,369 --> 00:00:50,847
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic,
Director Oh Seong Nam]

16
00:01:03,644 --> 00:01:05,168
[Do Not Enter, Investigation in Progress]

17
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:07,899
Ugh.

18
00:01:07,899 --> 00:01:10,023
They shot him in the eye again.
What's the deal?

19
00:01:10,023 --> 00:01:11,256
Did the bullet just happen to hit his eye?

20
00:01:11,256 --> 00:01:13,007
Or was it intentional?

21
00:01:13,007 --> 00:01:15,951
Twice in a row?
Then it had to be intentional.

22
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:19,067
Last time, the left eye. Today, the right.

23
00:01:19,067 --> 00:01:21,163
Wow. That's insane.

24
00:01:21,163 --> 00:01:23,551
Why would they do this when they
never even did it to the worst criminals...

25
00:01:23,551 --> 00:01:26,039
Are you sure you found nothing?

26
00:01:26,039 --> 00:01:28,135
Yeah. Nothing again.

27
00:01:28,135 --> 00:01:31,747
At most, he had a traffic fine
for running a light seven years ago.

28
00:01:31,747 --> 00:01:34,411
Anyway, is Kingfisher
seriously insane or what?

29
00:01:34,411 --> 00:01:37,690
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

30
00:01:43,611 --> 00:01:47,703
Wow, it's completely open outside.
Where on earth did the shot come from?

31
00:01:47,703 --> 00:01:50,290
Unless he flew through the air
to take the shot,

32
00:01:51,179 --> 00:01:52,738
he must've fired from across the river.

33
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:54,315
No way!

34
00:01:54,315 --> 00:01:57,090
From all the way over there?
Is that even possible?

35
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:25,375
<i>Another shooting has taken place
following last weekend's incident.</i>

36
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:26,831
[Another Fatal Shooting, Doctor in His 40s]
<i>The latest victim</i>

37
00:02:26,831 --> 00:02:28,951
[Shot Dead in Hospital Office]
<i>was a practicing doctor in his late 40s,</i>

38
00:02:28,951 --> 00:02:32,223
<i>who was killed
late yesterday afternoon in his clinic</i>

39
00:02:32,223 --> 00:02:34,607
[Good Deed Award, Oh Seong Nam]
<i>by a bullet that penetrated the window.</i>

40
00:02:34,607 --> 00:02:36,439
<i>He was pronounced dead at the scene.</i>

41
00:02:36,439 --> 00:02:39,575
<i>Just three days ago, a middle school teacher
in his 50s was shot dead</i>

42
00:02:39,575 --> 00:02:43,323
<i>while crossing a crosswalk
in broad daylight in the heart of the city.</i>

43
00:02:43,323 --> 00:02:46,231
<i>Now, another civilian
has been killed by gunfire,</i>

44
00:02:46,231 --> 00:02:48,667
<i>sending shockwaves across the country.</i>

45
00:02:48,667 --> 00:02:50,087
[Kingfisher Only Targeted Criminals]
<i>As this is the first time Kingfisher,</i>

46
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:51,755
[Why Kill Innocent Civilians?]
<i>which has only targeted criminals,</i>

47
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:54,667
[Hero or Murderer?]
<i>has gone after ordinary citizens,</i>

48
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:56,446
[Public Opinion Turns After Civilian Deaths]
<i>investigators are also looking closely</i>

49
00:02:56,446 --> 00:03:00,347
<i>into the identities of the two victims
and any connection between them.</i>

50
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,156
Who could have...

51
00:03:14,815 --> 00:03:19,199
Honey, I think Yul wants to show
her friends that she went to Jeju Island.

52
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,411
Let's show Daddy.

53
00:03:20,411 --> 00:03:22,111
Ta-da!

54
00:03:23,611 --> 00:03:26,511
Did you have that much fun
going on a trip with Mommy and Daddy?

55
00:03:26,511 --> 00:03:29,723
Yeah, it was so much fun.

56
00:03:29,723 --> 00:03:32,939
Yul, show this to your friends,
and then put it in your bag, okay?

57
00:03:32,939 --> 00:03:34,556
- Okay.
- Okay.

58
00:03:34,556 --> 00:03:36,839
Come on, put it on.

59
00:03:36,839 --> 00:03:40,595
Come on, let's go! Tangerine Girl.

60
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,295
Let's go!

61
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:44,911
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

62
00:03:44,935 --> 00:03:48,735
As previously reported,
neither victim had a criminal record,

63
00:03:48,735 --> 00:03:52,190
and no other criminal activity
has been identified.

64
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,283
Is there no connection
between the two victims?

65
00:03:55,283 --> 00:03:58,995
No. At this point, we haven't found
any connection between them.

66
00:03:58,995 --> 00:04:02,383
They have no overlap in hometowns,
schools, occupations, neighborhoods,

67
00:04:02,383 --> 00:04:04,890
or periods of military service.

68
00:04:06,019 --> 00:04:08,323
Have you identified the sniper locations?

69
00:04:09,547 --> 00:04:12,791
The first sniper location was
a building under construction.

70
00:04:12,791 --> 00:04:15,831
There were no CCTV cameras inside,
and the area outside has heavy foot traffic,

71
00:04:15,831 --> 00:04:18,555
making it difficult to identify a suspect.

72
00:04:18,555 --> 00:04:23,903
The second shot was fired from about
two kilometers across the Han River.

73
00:04:23,903 --> 00:04:25,836
Our forensic team
is currently tracking the shooter

74
00:04:25,836 --> 00:04:27,990
based on evidence from the scene.

75
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:34,599
Isn't it possible that
the shooter isn't Kingfisher?

76
00:04:34,599 --> 00:04:37,023
A copycat, for instance.

77
00:04:43,623 --> 00:04:46,399
Both cases clearly bear similarities
to the previous attacks:

78
00:04:46,399 --> 00:04:51,651
long-range shots, a single bullet,
and the location of the gunshot wound.

79
00:04:51,651 --> 00:04:54,335
But isn't the most important
difference the targets?

80
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:55,923
In the past 15 years,

81
00:04:55,923 --> 00:04:59,063
Kingfisher has never once
harmed an innocent civilian.

82
00:04:59,063 --> 00:05:01,631
Well, the nature of a crime
can change at any time.

83
00:05:01,631 --> 00:05:04,456
What matters is the method.

84
00:05:06,607 --> 00:05:10,595
Our task force considers Kingfisher
the prime suspect in both cases,

85
00:05:10,595 --> 00:05:12,707
no, in fact, effectively the only suspect,

86
00:05:12,707 --> 00:05:14,656
and we will do everything
we can to apprehend him.

87
00:05:14,656 --> 00:05:15,656
That's all.

88
00:05:15,682 --> 00:05:18,488
[Sniper locations]

89
00:05:30,103 --> 00:05:31,487
Ma'am,

90
00:05:31,487 --> 00:05:35,371
do you have any theory on why
he suddenly changed his targets?

91
00:05:35,371 --> 00:05:37,187
It's extremely rare for a serial killer

92
00:05:37,187 --> 00:05:39,907
like Kingfisher to suddenly
abandon his beliefs.

93
00:05:39,907 --> 00:05:44,190
Especially someone who's followed
such a consistent pattern for so long.

94
00:05:45,419 --> 00:05:48,156
If he's changed his targets, that means...

95
00:05:48,763 --> 00:05:51,490
the purpose behind the killings has changed.

96
00:05:53,359 --> 00:05:56,895
Well, let's wait and see
how the investigation develops.

97
00:05:56,895 --> 00:05:58,956
- Okay.
- Understood.

98
00:06:03,378 --> 00:06:04,167
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

99
00:06:04,399 --> 00:06:06,423
- Oh, one moment, please.
- Yeah.

100
00:06:07,863 --> 00:06:09,563
Where are you?

101
00:06:12,147 --> 00:06:14,027
Doesn't he seem a little down lately?

102
00:06:14,027 --> 00:06:15,468
Kingfisher's someone
he has spent years hunting

103
00:06:15,468 --> 00:06:16,803
in principle as a police officer.

104
00:06:16,803 --> 00:06:20,023
He's spent a long time
studying him in the process.

105
00:06:20,023 --> 00:06:24,056
He couldn't condone it,
but thought the guy drew the line.

106
00:06:25,559 --> 00:06:28,290
Maybe it's a little disillusioning
to see that change?

107
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:35,835
- What is it?
- A gift from Yul.

108
00:06:35,835 --> 00:06:37,535
A gift?

109
00:06:39,827 --> 00:06:41,995
You went to Jeju Island? When?

110
00:06:41,995 --> 00:06:44,695
Well... Last weekend, with my family.

111
00:06:46,479 --> 00:06:48,907
While some of us are working
our asses off without a single weekend off,

112
00:06:48,907 --> 00:06:50,856
you guys are out having fun.

113
00:06:52,063 --> 00:06:54,207
Yul's gift is so cute.

114
00:06:54,207 --> 00:06:55,251
So...

115
00:06:55,251 --> 00:06:59,859
While we were in Jeju Island,
Seoul was turned completely upside down.

116
00:06:59,859 --> 00:07:02,143
You must've been swamped, huh?

117
00:07:02,143 --> 00:07:05,859
You didn't bring a swamped person here
just to hand over this, right?

118
00:07:05,859 --> 00:07:10,923
You know I can't say anything
beyond the official briefing, right?

119
00:07:14,223 --> 00:07:18,023
Forget the official line.
What's your gut telling you?

120
00:07:20,235 --> 00:07:21,931
Hey.

121
00:07:21,931 --> 00:07:26,863
If there's another punk like Kingfisher
in this country, that's a tragedy.

122
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,890
That's your conclusion?

123
00:07:33,739 --> 00:07:37,627
I think you have a different opinion.

124
00:07:37,627 --> 00:07:40,011
You told me once before.

125
00:07:40,011 --> 00:07:43,827
You said, "Who knows when that gun
might be turned on an innocent person?"

126
00:07:43,827 --> 00:07:45,856
Do you still think that?

127
00:07:47,451 --> 00:07:50,127
What if someone killed them
out of personal revenge

128
00:07:50,127 --> 00:07:53,055
and framed Kingfisher for it?

129
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:56,356
Is that your conclusion?

130
00:07:58,455 --> 00:08:00,155
Wow.

131
00:08:03,155 --> 00:08:07,403
Why do I feel like
you're defending Kingfisher?

132
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,835
The same punk who threatened you, no less.

133
00:08:09,835 --> 00:08:10,983
If he were the kind of punk
who'd kill anyone,

134
00:08:10,983 --> 00:08:13,723
he would've killed me
instead of threatening me back then.

135
00:08:15,059 --> 00:08:17,407
Got any proof?

136
00:08:17,407 --> 00:08:20,123
Proof that Kingfisher was framed.

137
00:08:22,747 --> 00:08:24,790
That's what I'm going to find out now.

138
00:08:26,119 --> 00:08:29,423
You do your job. I'll do mine.

139
00:08:30,159 --> 00:08:31,859
I'm out.

140
00:08:37,379 --> 00:08:38,956
<i>I knew that punk
would cross the line someday.</i>

141
00:08:38,956 --> 00:08:40,759
<i>He's finally shown his true colors.</i>

142
00:08:40,759 --> 00:08:43,090
<i>A hero who catches criminals?
What a show-off.</i>

143
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:44,871
- <i>He's the criminal himself.</i>
- <i>True justice?</i>

144
00:08:44,871 --> 00:08:46,559
<i>Catching Kingfisher is justice.</i>

145
00:08:46,559 --> 00:08:48,479
<i>How are we supposed to live like this,
wondering when we'll get shot?</i>

146
00:08:48,479 --> 00:08:50,031
<i>What on earth are the police doing?
Why haven't they caught him yet?</i>

147
00:08:50,031 --> 00:08:52,323
People's views have totally changed.

148
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:53,973
The comments are all hate too.

149
00:08:53,973 --> 00:08:56,375
These people...

150
00:08:56,375 --> 00:08:58,756
How dare they compare
a fake to the real deal?

151
00:09:00,487 --> 00:09:03,611
Taking someone out with a single shot
from that distance and angle

152
00:09:03,611 --> 00:09:06,156
means he's a professional,
probably on Director Yoo's level.

153
00:09:06,156 --> 00:09:09,290
He's clearly someone who has no qualms

154
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:13,467
about sacrificing innocent people
to achieve his goal.

155
00:09:13,467 --> 00:09:16,255
What exactly is the point of all this?

156
00:09:16,255 --> 00:09:18,956
Kingfisher's social death?

157
00:09:25,395 --> 00:09:31,090
Instead of attacking me directly,
they're going after public opinion?

158
00:09:33,247 --> 00:09:35,790
If the goal is to turn
Kingfisher into a villain,

159
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:37,790
two victims won't be enough.

160
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:40,683
The more victims there are,
the greater the impact.

161
00:09:40,683 --> 00:09:44,090
We have to catch him
before there's a third victim.

162
00:09:44,090 --> 00:09:47,231
Ki Yeong Do,
did you look into what I asked for?

163
00:09:47,231 --> 00:09:49,347
It's ready.

164
00:09:49,347 --> 00:09:51,299
Here's the CCTV footage from the first case.

165
00:09:51,299 --> 00:09:54,523
This was taken just before the shooting.

166
00:09:54,523 --> 00:09:58,543
What's with that disabled man all bundled up?

167
00:09:58,543 --> 00:10:01,083
Isn't he hot in the middle of summer?

168
00:10:01,083 --> 00:10:03,235
Could he be deliberately hiding his face?

169
00:10:03,235 --> 00:10:07,239
Looks like the victim
approached him first to offer help.

170
00:10:07,239 --> 00:10:11,139
The victim had volunteered
with a disability organization before.

171
00:10:11,139 --> 00:10:16,091
He could've used that to lure
the victim to the sniper location.

172
00:10:16,091 --> 00:10:18,099
Your hunch was right.

173
00:10:18,099 --> 00:10:21,711
This is CCTV footage from outside
the hospital that morning.

174
00:10:21,711 --> 00:10:22,711
Oh, look!

175
00:10:22,711 --> 00:10:25,103
There's that man in the wheelchair again.

176
00:10:25,103 --> 00:10:26,839
Why would he go there?

177
00:10:26,839 --> 00:10:29,607
It doesn't look like he had
any particular role that day.

178
00:10:29,607 --> 00:10:31,356
"Catch me if you can."

179
00:10:40,207 --> 00:10:43,056
He's leaving us a trail to follow.

180
00:10:45,456 --> 00:10:47,375
All right. Let's follow it.

181
00:10:47,375 --> 00:10:51,343
Yeah. If we follow it, we'll eventually
find the killer's trail too.

182
00:10:51,343 --> 00:10:54,107
We have to find him
before there's another victim.

183
00:10:54,107 --> 00:10:55,483
You can do it, right?

184
00:10:55,483 --> 00:10:57,423
Yes, understood.

185
00:11:05,023 --> 00:11:08,035
We can't get into the scene.

186
00:11:08,035 --> 00:11:11,355
The hospital's probably closed anyway.

187
00:11:11,355 --> 00:11:13,607
Forget the scene.

188
00:11:13,607 --> 00:11:15,423
Let's start over there.

189
00:11:15,423 --> 00:11:17,139
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic]
Where?

190
00:11:17,139 --> 00:11:21,351
Do you know anything about
Dr. Oh Seong Nam, the director here?

191
00:11:21,351 --> 00:11:22,756
Oh Seong Nam?

192
00:11:22,756 --> 00:11:26,456
I haven't really heard anything about him.

193
00:11:28,331 --> 00:11:29,656
[Oh Seong Nam, Orthopedic Surgeon]

194
00:11:31,575 --> 00:11:33,614
- That's the CCTV camera outside, right?
- Yes.

195
00:11:33,614 --> 00:11:37,299
Can we check three days
of footage around the incident?

196
00:11:37,299 --> 00:11:42,051
Have you noticed anyone suspicious
hanging around here lately?

197
00:11:42,051 --> 00:11:43,751
No.

198
00:11:44,635 --> 00:11:45,635
Here you go.

199
00:11:45,635 --> 00:11:48,723
- We'll make a copy and return it.
- Sure.

200
00:11:49,032 --> 00:11:49,726
[Copying]

201
00:11:50,455 --> 00:11:53,359
Mr. Lee, they found
the second sniper location.

202
00:11:53,359 --> 00:11:55,655
Thank you.

203
00:11:55,655 --> 00:11:56,715
- Let's go.
- Right.

204
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,347
Dr. Oh Seong Nam.

205
00:11:58,347 --> 00:11:59,935
Oh, yes.

206
00:11:59,935 --> 00:12:04,535
Do you happen to remember
anyone who accompanied him?

207
00:12:04,535 --> 00:12:08,323
I'm not sure. Not really.

208
00:12:08,323 --> 00:12:13,119
Oh, I think they were mostly men
around his age.

209
00:12:13,119 --> 00:12:15,156
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

210
00:12:17,531 --> 00:12:21,375
Were they usually other doctors, then?

211
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:24,315
Well, I'm not sure about that...

212
00:12:24,315 --> 00:12:25,747
Is this the place?

213
00:12:25,747 --> 00:12:27,671
Yes. Based on the trajectory calculations,

214
00:12:27,671 --> 00:12:30,523
this is the only location
within the margin of error.

215
00:12:36,643 --> 00:12:38,471
The building was completed a few months ago,

216
00:12:38,471 --> 00:12:40,723
but it's still vacant,
so the CCTV wasn't operational.

217
00:12:40,723 --> 00:12:43,723
Wow. I don't know how he
managed to pick a place like this.

218
00:12:51,427 --> 00:12:52,867
Oh, but this is really strange.

219
00:12:52,867 --> 00:12:55,019
What is?

220
00:12:55,019 --> 00:12:56,983
There were no working CCTV cameras
at the first scene either.

221
00:12:56,983 --> 00:13:00,827
Why pick places like this
instead of wiping the footage like before?

222
00:13:00,827 --> 00:13:03,103
Something about this
just doesn't feel like Kingfisher...

223
00:13:03,103 --> 00:13:05,190
And what exactly is "like Kingfisher"?

224
00:13:05,190 --> 00:13:06,659
What?

225
00:13:06,659 --> 00:13:09,107
I mean, starting with the fact
that he's killing innocent people...

226
00:13:09,107 --> 00:13:11,143
Whether he killed guilty people
or innocent people,

227
00:13:11,143 --> 00:13:13,183
he killed someone. We have to catch him.

228
00:13:13,183 --> 00:13:15,251
We just need to do our jobs.

229
00:13:15,251 --> 00:13:16,956
Okay.

230
00:13:17,979 --> 00:13:21,256
We'll know once we catch him
whether he's Kingfisher or not.

231
00:13:24,307 --> 00:13:27,847
Looks like hair was found here too.
There was some over there as well.

232
00:13:27,847 --> 00:13:30,623
Weren't the sniper locations usually clean?

233
00:13:37,663 --> 00:13:42,656
Darn it, who on earth has a death wish?

234
00:13:47,631 --> 00:13:51,703
Darn it, how do I catch this punk?

235
00:13:51,703 --> 00:13:54,756
Just wait till I get my hands on him.

236
00:14:01,535 --> 00:14:03,688
Manager Tae Min,
why are you just sitting there?

237
00:14:03,688 --> 00:14:05,656
You need to do something!

238
00:14:08,727 --> 00:14:11,795
Our Kingfisher is about
to be branded a murderer.

239
00:14:11,795 --> 00:14:13,391
Her reputation is in the gutter!

240
00:14:13,391 --> 00:14:14,995
You two have been friends
since you were kids.

241
00:14:14,995 --> 00:14:16,807
And you're just going to sit there
like it's nothing?

242
00:14:16,807 --> 00:14:20,191
His movement pattern
confirms he was near the crime scene,

243
00:14:20,191 --> 00:14:21,763
though not on the day itself,
but a day or two before.

244
00:14:21,763 --> 00:14:23,475
Oh, what's he saying?

245
00:14:23,475 --> 00:14:25,939
<i>Okay, I'm here.</i>

246
00:14:26,111 --> 00:14:27,367
[Yoo Bo Na]

247
00:14:28,231 --> 00:14:29,859
What are you doing?

248
00:14:29,859 --> 00:14:31,756
Room 1803.

249
00:14:33,695 --> 00:14:36,156
Calm Oh Hyun Nam down.

250
00:14:37,390 --> 00:14:38,590
I'll put the key to good use.

251
00:14:38,614 --> 00:14:39,546
[Yoo Bo Na]

252
00:14:45,255 --> 00:14:47,623
So you were doing something after all.

253
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:50,190
You really are friends.

254
00:14:52,235 --> 00:14:54,856
But where did Director Yoo go?

255
00:14:56,571 --> 00:14:58,271
Huh?

256
00:15:32,671 --> 00:15:33,693
[Caller ID Restricted]

257
00:15:34,707 --> 00:15:38,139
<i>Surprise! Hi, my friend.</i>

258
00:15:38,139 --> 00:15:40,039
Changed your shoes?

259
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:43,267
It's too hot to keep wearing those.

260
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:46,663
Is there anything in the room?
Can you see me?

261
00:15:46,663 --> 00:15:48,115
Why ask?

262
00:15:48,115 --> 00:15:50,399
I know why you came.

263
00:15:50,399 --> 00:15:51,483
But it wasn't me.

264
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:54,775
I know. The shooting was pretty precise.

265
00:15:54,775 --> 00:15:58,223
You're actually pretty lousy
at sniping, aren't you?

266
00:15:59,439 --> 00:16:01,407
Only because you're a monster.

267
00:16:01,407 --> 00:16:03,523
<i>I'm not exactly lousy, you know.</i>

268
00:16:04,215 --> 00:16:06,375
Did Mama send you?

269
00:16:06,375 --> 00:16:09,056
<i>Mama would be hurt to hear that.</i>

270
00:16:09,783 --> 00:16:11,115
Then who is it?

271
00:16:11,115 --> 00:16:17,287
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

272
00:16:17,287 --> 00:16:18,987
<i>I'm busy.</i>

273
00:16:24,683 --> 00:16:27,690
I told you that you'd be the one
to come looking for me first.

274
00:17:23,983 --> 00:17:26,590
Seriously, these monsters...

275
00:17:28,167 --> 00:17:31,503
Yoo Bo Na better watch her back.

276
00:17:31,503 --> 00:17:33,503
[Funeral Hall]
Oh, these people just won't listen.

277
00:17:33,503 --> 00:17:35,867
Get out, seriously!

278
00:17:35,867 --> 00:17:39,603
If you come in here one more time,
I'm calling the police.

279
00:17:39,603 --> 00:17:41,551
Unbelievable, jeez...

280
00:17:41,551 --> 00:17:43,251
Go on in.

281
00:17:46,535 --> 00:17:50,467
In the end, we got kicked out
without even speaking to the family.

282
00:17:50,467 --> 00:17:51,843
At least we paid our respects.

283
00:17:51,843 --> 00:17:54,443
And we got a feel for the atmosphere inside.

284
00:17:54,443 --> 00:17:59,223
What, should we camp out at the entrance too?

285
00:18:02,871 --> 00:18:04,731
<i>They found Kingfisher's
second sniper location.</i>

286
00:18:04,731 --> 00:18:08,407
<i>Head over there. See if you can find
anything at the scene. Anything at all.</i>

287
00:18:08,407 --> 00:18:09,735
That was the Chief.

288
00:18:09,735 --> 00:18:12,863
He wants us to check if they found
anything at the second sniper location.

289
00:18:12,863 --> 00:18:17,715
The reporters camped out there
can cover it themselves.

290
00:18:17,715 --> 00:18:21,515
Let the police handle the shooter.
We'll look into the victims.

291
00:18:21,515 --> 00:18:24,356
Let's check out the first victim tomorrow.

292
00:18:24,356 --> 00:18:25,356
- Okay, sir.
- Well...

293
00:18:25,356 --> 00:18:27,590
He was an upstanding, law-abiding man.

294
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:30,091
He was kind to his patients.

295
00:18:30,091 --> 00:18:32,431
He must have been
a real family man at home too.

296
00:18:32,431 --> 00:18:34,590
He traveled abroad every year.

297
00:18:34,590 --> 00:18:39,463
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

298
00:18:39,463 --> 00:18:43,007
Why would anyone kill a man like that?
That darn Kingfisher.

299
00:18:43,007 --> 00:18:45,123
Jeez, what a punk.

300
00:18:46,755 --> 00:18:49,375
Not long ago they worshiped him as a hero,

301
00:18:49,375 --> 00:18:53,090
and now they treat him
like public enemy number one.

302
00:19:22,905 --> 00:19:24,100
[Tae Seong Chicken]

303
00:19:24,399 --> 00:19:26,099
Ms. Se Ah?

304
00:19:45,049 --> 00:19:45,955
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

305
00:19:45,979 --> 00:19:48,790
Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency?

306
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:51,027
[Going All the Way This Time,
Kingfisher Task Force Launched]

307
00:19:52,132 --> 00:19:53,329
[Past Cases Under Review
with New Investigative Techniques]

308
00:20:06,959 --> 00:20:09,171
What is this?

309
00:20:09,171 --> 00:20:10,790
Wait, don't tell me you made this yourself...

310
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:13,407
No, Sun Il did.

311
00:20:13,407 --> 00:20:16,731
I'm telling you again, I didn't make it.

312
00:20:16,731 --> 00:20:21,056
Sun Il made it to thank you
for boosting sales.

313
00:20:21,963 --> 00:20:23,447
Who cares who made it?

314
00:20:23,447 --> 00:20:25,807
Oh, I was craving something
spicy anyway. This is great.

315
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:27,279
I'll have to order more often.

316
00:20:27,279 --> 00:20:29,651
You really want to get deep-fried
instead of the chicken, huh?

317
00:20:29,651 --> 00:20:32,511
Why would someone craving
something spicy order chicken?

318
00:20:32,511 --> 00:20:34,147
I nearly died getting all the way here.

319
00:20:34,147 --> 00:20:35,979
Yum!

320
00:20:35,979 --> 00:20:36,995
Is it good?

321
00:20:36,995 --> 00:20:38,695
Yeah.

322
00:20:42,231 --> 00:20:43,371
So...

323
00:20:43,371 --> 00:20:45,659
is police work...

324
00:20:45,659 --> 00:20:48,056
really tough?

325
00:20:49,459 --> 00:20:51,355
Are you worried about me?

326
00:20:51,355 --> 00:20:52,723
Yeah.

327
00:20:52,723 --> 00:20:54,223
As if. You want to die?

328
00:20:54,223 --> 00:20:56,647
Yes or no? Just give me the facts.

329
00:20:56,647 --> 00:20:58,623
"Yes or no? Just give me the facts..."

330
00:21:03,375 --> 00:21:04,575
Huh?

331
00:21:04,575 --> 00:21:06,651
Assistant Manager Ki, what brings you here?

332
00:21:06,651 --> 00:21:09,919
Oh, well, you see.
I wasn't going from here to there.

333
00:21:09,919 --> 00:21:12,583
But I was going from there to here,
and then I saw the convenience store.

334
00:21:12,583 --> 00:21:14,671
I'm really thirsty.
They sell bottled water, right?

335
00:21:14,671 --> 00:21:16,790
Yes, they do. I suppose so.

336
00:21:22,655 --> 00:21:24,756
He came to the convenience store.

337
00:21:33,643 --> 00:21:34,711
Good to see you again.

338
00:21:34,711 --> 00:21:36,411
Indeed.

339
00:21:37,059 --> 00:21:40,690
You seem to really enjoy
butting into other people's business, huh?

340
00:21:41,355 --> 00:21:43,423
But I didn't butt in this time.

341
00:21:47,439 --> 00:21:49,495
You seem to be working yourself to the bone.

342
00:21:49,495 --> 00:21:52,503
Well, do you at least get overtime pay?

343
00:21:52,503 --> 00:21:56,711
Looks like you didn't even wash your hair.
Public service must be taking a toll.

344
00:21:56,711 --> 00:21:58,923
Don't they even let you eat?

345
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:01,967
I save time by skipping meals.

346
00:22:01,967 --> 00:22:04,011
We're after a very hot target these days.

347
00:22:04,011 --> 00:22:06,143
I hope you're not chasing the wrong shadow.

348
00:22:06,143 --> 00:22:07,415
And who do you think I'm talking about?

349
00:22:07,415 --> 00:22:10,190
The whole world is buzzing about him.

350
00:22:13,191 --> 00:22:15,371
You don't think it's Kingfisher?

351
00:22:15,371 --> 00:22:17,287
Because it's not his style.

352
00:22:17,287 --> 00:22:19,856
Even killers have a style?

353
00:22:21,567 --> 00:22:25,191
Professionally, we call it a "pattern."

354
00:22:25,191 --> 00:22:27,227
A pattern...

355
00:22:27,227 --> 00:22:30,295
Well, the targets have changed.

356
00:22:30,295 --> 00:22:31,563
That's why no message this time.

357
00:22:31,563 --> 00:22:34,167
He copied the method,
but something about it feels different.

358
00:22:34,167 --> 00:22:36,856
So you were thinking the same thing as me?

359
00:22:38,539 --> 00:22:40,667
I never said that.

360
00:22:40,667 --> 00:22:42,891
Your face did.

361
00:22:42,891 --> 00:22:46,656
I'm pretty good at reading people.

362
00:22:49,819 --> 00:22:54,456
Well, sounds like you two
are on the same page.

363
00:22:54,456 --> 00:22:59,103
Now that you're done,
can I make a bombshell announcement?

364
00:22:59,103 --> 00:23:01,627
- A bombshell...
- Announcement?

365
00:23:01,627 --> 00:23:03,327
I'm...

366
00:23:04,983 --> 00:23:06,556
going to become a cop.

367
00:23:06,556 --> 00:23:08,923
I'm going to become a cop.

368
00:23:08,923 --> 00:23:09,995
- What?
- What did you say?

369
00:23:09,995 --> 00:23:13,687
I'm going to become a cop
and catch all the...

370
00:23:13,687 --> 00:23:15,379
- bad guys.
- Wait, why of all things...

371
00:23:15,379 --> 00:23:17,123
Seriously? Awesome!

372
00:23:18,671 --> 00:23:20,036
Is that something to be happy about?

373
00:23:20,036 --> 00:23:22,205
- Then should I try to stop her?
- Of course!

374
00:23:22,205 --> 00:23:24,095
- Why?
- Well...

375
00:23:24,095 --> 00:23:26,571
Because being a cop is dangerous.

376
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:28,190
Who? The criminals?

377
00:23:28,190 --> 00:23:31,103
And she'd have to study for years
just to pass the exam.

378
00:23:31,103 --> 00:23:33,103
Oh, there's also a special recruitment
program for martial artists.

379
00:23:33,103 --> 00:23:34,947
Really? They have that?

380
00:23:34,947 --> 00:23:36,187
- Look, Se Ah.
- Yes.

381
00:23:36,187 --> 00:23:37,290
- What?
- If you look around,

382
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:39,191
- you could find...
- I'm rooting for you, Kwon Se Dol!

383
00:23:39,191 --> 00:23:40,827
You know I'll be your senior
if you become a cop, right?

384
00:23:40,827 --> 00:23:42,055
Oh, shut up!

385
00:23:42,055 --> 00:23:44,556
Special recruitment for martial artists?
How does that work?

386
00:23:44,556 --> 00:23:47,939
Here's how you do it.
Well, the competition's pretty stiff.

387
00:23:47,939 --> 00:23:50,359
Having a medal from an international
competition would give you an advantage.

388
00:23:50,359 --> 00:23:51,532
- You don't have one.
- No, but I've won

389
00:23:51,532 --> 00:23:52,556
plenty of domestic competitions.

390
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:53,969
Really? Then your next shot would be

391
00:23:53,969 --> 00:23:55,623
the Commissioner General's Cup competition...

392
00:23:59,409 --> 00:24:01,627
Oh, this is nice.

393
00:24:04,419 --> 00:24:07,088
What made you make such a drastic decision?

394
00:24:07,827 --> 00:24:09,623
Was it because of your friend?

395
00:24:09,623 --> 00:24:13,523
Oh, well, he did have some influence.

396
00:24:13,523 --> 00:24:18,975
But more than that, I think
being a police officer is a great job.

397
00:24:18,975 --> 00:24:21,723
But why all of a sudden...

398
00:24:22,971 --> 00:24:27,739
It felt like my heart was racing.

399
00:24:27,739 --> 00:24:31,067
When I caught those attackers last time.

400
00:24:31,067 --> 00:24:35,123
And when I caught that
voice phishing scammer recently.

401
00:24:37,659 --> 00:24:43,023
The other day, Assistant Manager Ki,
when you told me you loved me.

402
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:44,023
Back then, I...

403
00:24:44,023 --> 00:24:46,256
Oh, I know.

404
00:24:46,256 --> 00:24:48,890
You didn't mean anything by it.
You were just saying it casually.

405
00:24:48,890 --> 00:24:54,711
Who'd seriously say that to a woman
they've only met a few times?

406
00:24:54,711 --> 00:24:58,423
That night, I happened to run into Seong Hun.

407
00:24:58,423 --> 00:25:00,317
I asked him to go to a PC bang with me,

408
00:25:00,317 --> 00:25:03,447
but he said he had work
the next day and left.

409
00:25:03,447 --> 00:25:07,579
At first, I found him a bit annoying,
but then it suddenly hit me...

410
00:25:07,579 --> 00:25:10,751
"Oh, I'm this old,

411
00:25:10,751 --> 00:25:15,027
but I don't even
have a job to go to, no career,

412
00:25:15,027 --> 00:25:18,375
and I'm not pulling my weight in society."

413
00:25:18,375 --> 00:25:20,923
Aren't you in grad school?

414
00:25:21,759 --> 00:25:25,411
I just went to grad school
because it was related to my major.

415
00:25:25,411 --> 00:25:28,723
I was wondering
what I should do with my life,

416
00:25:28,723 --> 00:25:32,451
and then I remembered that moment.

417
00:25:32,451 --> 00:25:39,290
How my heart raced
when I caught those bad guys.

418
00:25:40,991 --> 00:25:46,491
I'm not particularly good at anything,
and judo is all I really have.

419
00:25:46,491 --> 00:25:48,211
But if I keep using it,

420
00:25:48,211 --> 00:25:53,690
maybe I can help
make the world a little better?

421
00:25:55,101 --> 00:26:00,839
Se Ah, do you believe the law
and the police can protect everyone?

422
00:26:00,839 --> 00:26:04,783
Unless you're the police,
you can't catch criminals.

423
00:26:04,783 --> 00:26:07,211
And there's no other way
to punish them by law, right?

424
00:26:07,211 --> 00:26:09,011
What if there were another way?

425
00:26:09,011 --> 00:26:12,473
- What?
- Maybe somewhere in this world,

426
00:26:12,473 --> 00:26:15,183
there are people who do that
in a different way.

427
00:26:15,183 --> 00:26:18,840
With the same goal of
making the world a better place,

428
00:26:18,840 --> 00:26:21,935
protecting the people
the police fail to protect,

429
00:26:21,935 --> 00:26:25,023
and punishing those who escape punishment

430
00:26:27,420 --> 00:26:29,120
under the law.

431
00:26:55,030 --> 00:27:00,856
<i>Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?</i>

432
00:27:17,545 --> 00:27:20,475
Yul is finally asleep.
I read her two whole books.

433
00:27:20,475 --> 00:27:23,223
No wonder. I thought you dozed off with her.

434
00:27:23,223 --> 00:27:26,447
Honey, once we finish this,
we're done for the day.

435
00:27:26,447 --> 00:27:29,223
Then shall we have something cold to drink?

436
00:27:30,497 --> 00:27:32,647
How about a beer?

437
00:27:32,647 --> 00:27:34,356
- Beer?
- Yeah.

438
00:27:36,883 --> 00:27:41,139
I heard a beer after putting the kids to bed
tastes like heaven.

439
00:27:41,139 --> 00:27:42,923
- Putting the kids to bed?
- Yeah.

440
00:27:43,686 --> 00:27:44,715
Clocking out of parenting?

441
00:27:44,715 --> 00:27:49,415
So this is what they say washes away
all the day's stress and exhaustion.

442
00:27:49,415 --> 00:27:51,456
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

443
00:27:53,490 --> 00:27:55,490
Oh, that's refreshing.

444
00:27:56,739 --> 00:28:00,523
Oh, it feels like all that
pent-up stress just melts away.

445
00:28:04,756 --> 00:28:07,590
Now I see why people love drinking this.

446
00:28:09,399 --> 00:28:13,656
But you know what? Yul seems
really fascinated by her first plane ride.

447
00:28:13,656 --> 00:28:15,499
She's been talking about it all day.

448
00:28:15,499 --> 00:28:17,943
"Mommy, we flew through the sky, right?"

449
00:28:17,943 --> 00:28:20,915
"The fluffy clouds were
so pretty, weren't they?"

450
00:28:20,915 --> 00:28:23,590
"And we saw the ocean
from up in the sky, too, right?"

451
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:26,859
Luckily, she wasn't scared of flying at all.

452
00:28:26,859 --> 00:28:29,031
We'll have to take her
on another flight soon.

453
00:28:29,031 --> 00:28:33,451
Yul is pretty... active, you know?

454
00:28:33,451 --> 00:28:34,723
And she's not easily scared.

455
00:28:34,723 --> 00:28:38,387
Maybe she should try something
a little more active, don't you think?

456
00:28:38,387 --> 00:28:40,123
For example, like...

457
00:28:41,559 --> 00:28:43,223
swimming,

458
00:28:44,231 --> 00:28:46,918
taekwondo, or skiing?

459
00:28:46,918 --> 00:28:49,856
Is snowboarding a little wilder than skiing?

460
00:28:49,856 --> 00:28:51,923
She likes scary things.

461
00:28:51,923 --> 00:28:54,090
- What about you?
- Huh?

462
00:28:56,059 --> 00:28:58,456
Don't you have anything you want to do?

463
00:29:00,319 --> 00:29:05,123
I've done everything
I wanted to try since I met you.

464
00:29:08,449 --> 00:29:11,343
Which one did you like best?

465
00:29:11,343 --> 00:29:13,623
I loved them all.

466
00:29:13,623 --> 00:29:15,323
I loved every moment.

467
00:29:18,263 --> 00:29:23,112
Walking hand in hand with you and chatting
as we walked through the flowers.

468
00:29:23,112 --> 00:29:26,290
And all those picnics by the Han River.

469
00:29:26,290 --> 00:29:30,795
And every Sunday, you being the chef
making black bean noodles?

470
00:29:30,795 --> 00:29:35,487
And all those late-night
horror movies you hated.

471
00:29:35,487 --> 00:29:38,515
All the pretty selfies we took together.

472
00:29:38,515 --> 00:29:40,215
All those things.

473
00:29:42,079 --> 00:29:45,090
Well, those are all such ordinary things.

474
00:29:45,823 --> 00:29:48,290
They're all special to me.

475
00:29:49,775 --> 00:29:53,290
There's still so much I want to do with you.

476
00:29:54,411 --> 00:29:56,111
Really?

477
00:29:57,135 --> 00:30:03,756
Something we haven't done before.
Something better and more special.

478
00:30:04,383 --> 00:30:08,587
Let's do every single one of them together.

479
00:30:09,595 --> 00:30:11,431
Yeah.

480
00:30:11,431 --> 00:30:13,223
Together.

481
00:30:16,619 --> 00:30:18,319
Shall we drink?

482
00:30:34,359 --> 00:30:36,001
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

483
00:30:46,239 --> 00:30:47,590
[Trace Evidence Analysis Report]
Mr. Lee, these are the analysis results

484
00:30:47,590 --> 00:30:49,490
for the trace evidence from the scenes.

485
00:30:50,939 --> 00:30:52,035
No way!

486
00:30:52,035 --> 00:30:53,363
Why? What is it?

487
00:30:53,363 --> 00:30:57,056
They found hair with matching DNA
at both sniper locations?

488
00:30:57,835 --> 00:31:00,583
- What?
- No match in the police database...

489
00:31:00,583 --> 00:31:02,883
But is there any basic profile?
What about the gender?

490
00:31:02,883 --> 00:31:04,431
Oh, here it is!

491
00:31:04,431 --> 00:31:07,690
Female, estimated to be in her 30s?

492
00:31:10,735 --> 00:31:12,687
Wow. What is this?

493
00:31:12,687 --> 00:31:14,387
[Female, Estimated 30s]
If it's a woman...

494
00:31:15,128 --> 00:31:17,923
Could it be the person that pickpocket saw?

495
00:31:21,171 --> 00:31:23,197
We entered the man's build, clothing,

496
00:31:23,197 --> 00:31:24,443
and wheelchair details
into the search program

497
00:31:24,443 --> 00:31:27,247
and tracked his movements
on CCTV over several days.

498
00:31:27,247 --> 00:31:28,771
I found something unusual.

499
00:31:28,771 --> 00:31:30,471
What is it?

500
00:31:31,235 --> 00:31:35,856
He kept going around this area,
so I tracked his movements.

501
00:31:37,075 --> 00:31:39,123
This is what I found.

502
00:31:40,331 --> 00:31:43,359
He went onto that island
and circled its perimeter several times.

503
00:31:43,359 --> 00:31:45,487
I think it might be some kind of message.

504
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:48,427
The bottom looks like a crescent moon.

505
00:31:48,427 --> 00:31:52,619
The top is the eye,
and the bottom is the eyebrow?

506
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,211
Could it be something like that?

507
00:31:54,211 --> 00:31:57,619
The victims, the eyes.

508
00:31:58,659 --> 00:32:00,511
Oh, you're right.

509
00:32:00,511 --> 00:32:05,091
Both victims were shot in the eye
this time, weren't they?

510
00:32:05,091 --> 00:32:10,475
According to our internal police network,
could this be connected to the case?

511
00:32:10,475 --> 00:32:13,456
The vital spot of every beast

512
00:32:14,279 --> 00:32:15,979
is the eye.

513
00:32:22,647 --> 00:32:28,456
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

514
00:32:29,931 --> 00:32:32,647
How long will it take
to trace a restricted number?

515
00:32:32,647 --> 00:32:34,472
If the original number
is still recorded in the network,

516
00:32:34,472 --> 00:32:36,059
it could take as little as 15 minutes.

517
00:32:36,059 --> 00:32:37,990
I need it within ten minutes.

518
00:32:39,783 --> 00:32:41,556
Sooner if possible.

519
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:54,323
Where are you now?

520
00:33:09,949 --> 00:33:13,990
[Summer 2008, Russia]

521
00:33:27,299 --> 00:33:28,471
The boss is having dinner.

522
00:33:28,471 --> 00:33:30,227
He's having a late dinner, huh?

523
00:33:30,227 --> 00:33:34,775
How can a punk who slaughtered
an entire family stomach his food?

524
00:33:34,775 --> 00:33:36,771
It's a waste of good food.

525
00:33:36,771 --> 00:33:38,323
Let's finish this and go.

526
00:33:38,323 --> 00:33:41,143
Even death row inmates get a last meal.

527
00:33:41,143 --> 00:33:42,331
Just wait.

528
00:33:42,331 --> 00:33:46,056
That's your problem.

529
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:49,723
If it's too much trouble, I can do it.

530
00:33:50,395 --> 00:33:53,923
A punk like that deserves
a bullet right in the eye...

531
00:34:00,731 --> 00:34:02,455
Haven't seen that before.

532
00:34:02,455 --> 00:34:04,771
Oh, this?

533
00:34:04,771 --> 00:34:07,467
I liked it, so I got one tattooed.

534
00:34:07,467 --> 00:34:09,427
It's just like that saying.

535
00:34:09,427 --> 00:34:12,439
The vital spot of every beast

536
00:34:12,439 --> 00:34:13,683
is the eye.

537
00:34:13,683 --> 00:34:16,223
How is it? Pretty awesome, right?

538
00:34:17,163 --> 00:34:19,090
Keep an eye on the surroundings.

539
00:34:19,990 --> 00:34:21,080
Dinner's over.

540
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,780
He's leaving.

541
00:34:35,715 --> 00:34:36,919
Mission accomplished.

542
00:34:36,919 --> 00:34:38,663
Good work.

543
00:34:38,663 --> 00:34:40,363
Clean up and come back.

544
00:34:50,456 --> 00:34:53,556
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

545
00:34:53,556 --> 00:34:54,590
You must be the boss's daughter.

546
00:34:54,590 --> 00:34:56,690
Layla, wait, let me handle...

547
00:35:06,419 --> 00:35:08,379
Are you insane?

548
00:35:08,379 --> 00:35:09,883
Do you have any idea what you've done?

549
00:35:09,883 --> 00:35:12,415
What? Shot a kid?

550
00:35:12,415 --> 00:35:14,290
Or shot her in the eye?

551
00:35:18,215 --> 00:35:21,603
"Eliminate any witnesses immediately."

552
00:35:21,603 --> 00:35:23,495
I was just following orders.

553
00:35:23,495 --> 00:35:27,023
Isn't the eye a witness's vital spot?

554
00:35:27,695 --> 00:35:30,656
Who on earth gave that kind of order?

555
00:35:31,711 --> 00:35:36,663
"Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone."

556
00:35:36,663 --> 00:35:41,923
"But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children."

557
00:35:48,675 --> 00:35:50,256
She was just a child.

558
00:35:50,256 --> 00:35:53,035
She had no weapon and didn't even scream.

559
00:35:53,035 --> 00:35:55,671
She was just a scared little girl.

560
00:35:55,671 --> 00:35:58,183
I heard she was his daughter.

561
00:35:58,183 --> 00:35:59,831
The child was innocent.

562
00:35:59,831 --> 00:36:04,423
Her dad killed countless innocent people.

563
00:36:04,423 --> 00:36:06,090
Some of them were children too.

564
00:36:06,090 --> 00:36:08,456
You used to say it all the time.

565
00:36:08,456 --> 00:36:11,351
I thought you just meant it as a warning.

566
00:36:11,351 --> 00:36:13,355
We've never done anything like this.

567
00:36:13,355 --> 00:36:15,571
Because we'd never been caught.

568
00:36:15,571 --> 00:36:19,167
A witness eventually becomes a voice.

569
00:36:19,167 --> 00:36:21,590
And that voice calls for revenge.

570
00:36:24,807 --> 00:36:27,090
You could've been killed.

571
00:36:29,307 --> 00:36:32,303
Then you should've killed me instead.

572
00:36:32,303 --> 00:36:35,103
"Those children are safe now."

573
00:36:35,103 --> 00:36:37,723
"You saved them."

574
00:36:37,723 --> 00:36:42,279
You said that to me when I was eight.

575
00:36:42,279 --> 00:36:44,375
- I did.
- I don't recall anywhere

576
00:36:44,375 --> 00:36:48,663
in those words saying it's okay
to kill innocent people to save someone.

577
00:36:48,663 --> 00:36:50,363
Is that so?

578
00:36:54,323 --> 00:36:59,103
Today, we broke the most important rule
we're supposed to uphold.

579
00:36:59,103 --> 00:37:01,556
You don't see it the way I do, Mama.

580
00:37:02,207 --> 00:37:03,907
Am I right?

581
00:37:06,399 --> 00:37:08,099
So?

582
00:37:11,383 --> 00:37:16,099
Thank you for raising me
and teaching me all these years.

583
00:37:16,099 --> 00:37:19,390
I thought I'd get the chance
to repay you someday.

584
00:37:25,419 --> 00:37:27,123
Take care of yourself.

585
00:37:37,265 --> 00:37:39,544
You tracked me down faster than I thought.

586
00:37:40,397 --> 00:37:42,677
You already knew.

587
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:45,377
That's why you came to Korea.

588
00:37:47,453 --> 00:37:49,297
Are you helping her?

589
00:37:49,297 --> 00:37:51,212
Or hunting her?

590
00:37:53,389 --> 00:37:55,945
Losing her every single time?

591
00:37:57,429 --> 00:38:00,212
Seoul is bigger than I thought, isn't it?

592
00:38:01,485 --> 00:38:03,581
What's the reason?

593
00:38:03,581 --> 00:38:06,421
The reason Layla's doing this to me.

594
00:38:06,421 --> 00:38:09,445
In short? Or the long version?

595
00:38:10,917 --> 00:38:12,878
The short version?

596
00:38:15,937 --> 00:38:18,078
Well, resentment toward you?

597
00:38:22,257 --> 00:38:24,112
What do you mean?

598
00:38:24,717 --> 00:38:25,909
Why would she resent me?

599
00:38:25,909 --> 00:38:27,845
Unintentionally,

600
00:38:28,457 --> 00:38:30,712
I happened to see something.

601
00:38:31,913 --> 00:38:34,103
<i>When I heard you two were working together,</i>

602
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:38,678
<i>I got curious and followed you that day
without you knowing.</i>

603
00:38:42,037 --> 00:38:46,797
<i>She clearly saw that girl,
but why hasn't she told you?</i>

604
00:38:46,797 --> 00:38:49,393
- Mission accomplished.
- Good work.

605
00:38:49,393 --> 00:38:51,093
Clean up and come back.

606
00:38:55,557 --> 00:38:58,065
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

607
00:38:58,065 --> 00:39:00,812
- You must be the boss's daughter.
- Layla, wait, let me handle...

608
00:39:03,201 --> 00:39:05,078
<i>I realized in that moment.</i>

609
00:39:05,078 --> 00:39:06,849
<i>That girl was nothing</i>

610
00:39:06,849 --> 00:39:10,178
- <i>but prey caught in Layla's trap.</i>
- Are you insane?

611
00:39:10,178 --> 00:39:12,909
<i>Layla deliberately let that girl see you.</i>

612
00:39:12,909 --> 00:39:14,609
Take care of yourself.

613
00:39:29,933 --> 00:39:34,613
If you're going to look like you just
lost an arm, you should've stopped her.

614
00:39:34,613 --> 00:39:38,397
She started this life
by her own will and choice.

615
00:39:38,397 --> 00:39:42,145
I promised she could leave
whenever she wanted.

616
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:48,481
Why didn't you tell her?

617
00:39:48,481 --> 00:39:50,812
That you never gave the order?

618
00:39:52,097 --> 00:39:53,612
Because I wasn't sure.

619
00:39:53,612 --> 00:39:57,217
Because I wasn't sure I could give

620
00:39:57,217 --> 00:40:02,889
the same order
if a witness actually appeared.

621
00:40:02,889 --> 00:40:05,917
A mentor trying to protect her disciple,

622
00:40:05,917 --> 00:40:09,745
and a disciple who'd rather die herself.

623
00:40:12,029 --> 00:40:14,245
It wouldn't have lasted much longer anyway.

624
00:40:16,257 --> 00:40:20,378
Sometimes, she was my mentor too.

625
00:40:22,057 --> 00:40:24,012
Take care of her from now on.

626
00:40:25,817 --> 00:40:27,377
Take care of what?

627
00:40:27,377 --> 00:40:28,561
Yoo Bo Na.

628
00:40:28,561 --> 00:40:31,669
Where she goes, what she does,

629
00:40:31,669 --> 00:40:33,069
and whether she's safe.

630
00:40:33,069 --> 00:40:36,473
Layla was kicked out of
the organization over that.

631
00:40:36,473 --> 00:40:41,537
She moved to Southeast Asia and now
works as a hired killer, quite in demand.

632
00:40:41,537 --> 00:40:45,381
You know what that is, right?
Getting paid to kill people.

633
00:40:45,381 --> 00:40:49,445
Then we recently learned
she'd returned to Korea.

634
00:40:50,493 --> 00:40:52,613
Did Mama send you?

635
00:40:52,613 --> 00:40:55,421
Sorry for being so messed up all this time.

636
00:40:55,421 --> 00:40:59,229
My mom cherishes her disciple
more than her own son,

637
00:40:59,229 --> 00:41:02,137
so can't the son get a little salty about it?

638
00:41:02,137 --> 00:41:04,412
If Kingfisher was the first target,

639
00:41:05,942 --> 00:41:08,041
I must be next.

640
00:41:08,041 --> 00:41:10,145
Well,

641
00:41:10,145 --> 00:41:13,678
do you really think
I don't know what you know?

642
00:41:18,561 --> 00:41:20,478
Your Achilles' heels.

643
00:41:23,421 --> 00:41:26,161
Don't you ever think about coming back?

644
00:41:26,161 --> 00:41:27,721
Mama...

645
00:41:27,721 --> 00:41:30,145
I think she's still waiting for you.

646
00:41:32,897 --> 00:41:35,012
You said you sent her my info.

647
00:41:35,669 --> 00:41:37,641
She probably already knows.

648
00:41:37,641 --> 00:41:39,912
That I'm not coming back.

649
00:41:42,193 --> 00:41:43,978
Give her my regards.

650
00:41:49,081 --> 00:41:51,445
She must be very disappointed.

651
00:41:55,693 --> 00:41:57,361
Did you find her?

652
00:41:57,361 --> 00:41:59,441
No. I'll go myself.

653
00:41:59,441 --> 00:42:01,712
Send me the location.

654
00:42:29,977 --> 00:42:33,433
Ms. Hee Seon, yeah. You're with Yul, right?

655
00:42:33,433 --> 00:42:35,612
Oh, yeah. We just left the daycare.

656
00:42:35,612 --> 00:42:37,061
Did anything seem strange?

657
00:42:37,061 --> 00:42:39,457
Like anyone suspicious hanging around.

658
00:42:39,457 --> 00:42:41,869
No, not at all. Why? Why do you ask?

659
00:42:41,869 --> 00:42:43,273
Oh, it's nothing.

660
00:42:43,273 --> 00:42:47,349
Could you go straight home?
I'm coming to pick her up now.

661
00:42:47,349 --> 00:42:49,512
Okay. Let's go.

662
00:42:50,402 --> 00:42:51,600
[My Heart]

663
00:43:21,737 --> 00:43:23,709
Someone once asked me...

664
00:43:23,709 --> 00:43:25,321
<i>What if...</i>

665
00:43:25,321 --> 00:43:29,345
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

666
00:43:30,709 --> 00:43:32,409
I don't know.

667
00:43:33,213 --> 00:43:35,278
I've never thought about it.

668
00:43:36,529 --> 00:43:38,097
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

669
00:43:38,097 --> 00:43:42,845
Actually, I sometimes imagine
a life without Tae Seong.

670
00:43:44,305 --> 00:43:47,945
And every time, I can't picture anything.

671
00:43:48,565 --> 00:43:50,845
Just like...

672
00:43:50,845 --> 00:43:53,212
my heart has stopped.

673
00:43:53,897 --> 00:43:55,345
<i>Life without Tae Seong...</i>

674
00:43:55,345 --> 00:43:56,445
[My Heart]

675
00:43:56,445 --> 00:43:59,609
<i>would be like death, right?</i>

676
00:43:59,609 --> 00:44:01,112
<i>Because I love him.</i>

677
00:44:01,112 --> 00:44:02,353
[Big Precious]

678
00:44:02,353 --> 00:44:04,412
<i>Because I love him so much.</i>

679
00:44:04,436 --> 00:44:05,809
[My Heart]

680
00:44:15,242 --> 00:44:16,601
How long has he been inside?

681
00:44:16,601 --> 00:44:18,821
He went in five minutes ago.
He hasn't come out yet.

682
00:44:18,821 --> 00:44:20,521
Really?

683
00:44:35,509 --> 00:44:37,985
Darn it, this punk...

684
00:44:37,985 --> 00:44:39,712
He walked right out.

685
00:44:44,674 --> 00:44:46,221
[Not Today]

686
00:44:47,659 --> 00:44:48,556
[Team Leader Bong]

687
00:44:48,961 --> 00:44:50,153
Yes, Team Leader.

688
00:44:50,153 --> 00:44:52,761
We lost him. The wheelchair was a fake.

689
00:44:52,761 --> 00:44:54,461
What?

690
00:45:29,205 --> 00:45:31,025
Tae Seong!

691
00:45:31,025 --> 00:45:33,527
Honey, what brings you here?

692
00:45:33,527 --> 00:45:34,934
Why weren't you answering your phone?

693
00:45:34,934 --> 00:45:36,452
- I called you several times.
- My phone?

694
00:45:36,452 --> 00:45:39,645
I must've left it at the office.
Sorry, but what's up? Is something wrong?

695
00:45:39,645 --> 00:45:41,581
No, nothing's wrong.

696
00:45:41,581 --> 00:45:44,285
Well, actually... It's just that, honey.

697
00:45:44,285 --> 00:45:48,212
Someone I know said they were sending me
a package, so I gave them an address.

698
00:45:48,212 --> 00:45:51,133
Then I realized I'd stupidly
given them your office address.

699
00:45:51,133 --> 00:45:52,525
You did?

700
00:45:52,525 --> 00:45:54,812
So I called you a few times,
but you didn't answer.

701
00:45:54,812 --> 00:45:57,463
So I was passing by and thought
I'd stop in and see you.

702
00:45:57,463 --> 00:45:59,109
- Sorry to bother you while you're busy.
- No, it's fine.

703
00:45:59,109 --> 00:46:00,153
You came out to get it?

704
00:46:00,153 --> 00:46:02,057
Of course, I did. It's totally fine.

705
00:46:02,057 --> 00:46:03,641
- Sorry.
- It's fine. Don't worry.

706
00:46:03,641 --> 00:46:06,123
- I should get back to work.
- Okay.

707
00:46:06,123 --> 00:46:08,212
- Take care.
- Bye!

708
00:46:11,981 --> 00:46:13,012
- Honey.
- Yeah?

709
00:46:13,012 --> 00:46:14,945
Why does it feel so hard to leave?

710
00:46:15,549 --> 00:46:17,009
Are you working late tonight?

711
00:46:17,009 --> 00:46:18,507
I have some outside work,
but it should end early.

712
00:46:18,507 --> 00:46:20,178
I'll come home early.

713
00:46:21,489 --> 00:46:25,278
Okay. See you at home.
I really should go, as much as I hate to.

714
00:47:16,841 --> 00:47:21,381
<i>Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone.</i>

715
00:47:21,381 --> 00:47:26,741
<i>But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children.</i>

716
00:47:26,741 --> 00:47:28,912
<i>Layla, wait, let me handle...</i>

717
00:47:34,402 --> 00:47:36,354
[Ms. Hee Seon]

718
00:47:37,217 --> 00:47:39,612
Yeah, Ms. Hee Seon, are you home now?

719
00:47:39,612 --> 00:47:41,197
You're with Yul, right?

720
00:47:41,197 --> 00:47:43,025
Bo Na, I can't find Yul anywhere!

721
00:47:43,025 --> 00:47:44,837
<i>What should I do?</i>

722
00:47:44,837 --> 00:47:46,021
As reported earlier,

723
00:47:46,021 --> 00:47:49,529
hair with matching DNA was found
at both sniper locations.

724
00:47:49,529 --> 00:47:54,245
The NFS analysis indicates
it belongs to a woman in her 30s.

725
00:48:05,465 --> 00:48:07,517
Please zoom in there.

726
00:48:07,517 --> 00:48:09,033
<i>Accordingly, we narrowed the suspect pool</i>

727
00:48:09,033 --> 00:48:10,633
[Suspect Pool Narrowed Down]
to women in their 30s.

728
00:48:10,633 --> 00:48:14,949
After rechecking CCTV and dashcam footage
collected around the crime scenes,

729
00:48:14,949 --> 00:48:19,045
we found one woman
who was present at both scenes.

730
00:48:19,045 --> 00:48:20,493
Is she really the same person?

731
00:48:20,493 --> 00:48:22,845
Her clothes and shoes are all different.

732
00:48:27,621 --> 00:48:32,193
As you can see, she has
the same tattoo in the same spot.

733
00:48:32,193 --> 00:48:34,873
A crescent moon below and an eye above.

734
00:48:34,873 --> 00:48:39,212
As you know, both victims
were shot in the eye.

735
00:48:40,229 --> 00:48:43,761
A dashcam from a car parked near
the second crime scene captured this woman

736
00:48:43,761 --> 00:48:46,678
[A Woman Gets in a Car and Drives Off]
getting into a car and driving off.

737
00:48:46,678 --> 00:48:48,269
[Zoom in on License Plate]
We ran the plate,

738
00:48:48,269 --> 00:48:49,628
[Owner: A Man in His 70s]
and the owner turned out to be a man

739
00:48:49,628 --> 00:48:51,057
[Who Died Three Years Ago]
in his 70s who died three years ago.

740
00:48:51,057 --> 00:48:52,841
So it's a stolen-identity car.

741
00:48:52,841 --> 00:48:53,985
Well, that's undeniable proof.

742
00:48:53,985 --> 00:48:55,697
[Seoul Traffic Control Center]
<i>We're using every available resource</i>

743
00:48:55,697 --> 00:48:57,833
<i>to track down the vehicle,
including the AI-powered integrated system</i>

744
00:48:57,833 --> 00:49:00,929
<i>for searching wanted vehicles
and intelligent CCTV systems</i>

745
00:49:00,929 --> 00:49:03,445
<i>operated by local governments.</i>

746
00:49:15,364 --> 00:49:17,064
Ugh.

747
00:49:21,361 --> 00:49:24,178
<i>It's been delivered.</i>

748
00:49:47,469 --> 00:49:48,873
Please spare me.

749
00:49:48,873 --> 00:49:50,777
Please, spare my life.

750
00:49:50,777 --> 00:49:55,281
If you want to live,
tell me what I want to hear.

751
00:49:55,281 --> 00:49:57,749
Oh... I really don't know anything.

752
00:49:57,749 --> 00:50:01,245
I've never even seen them.
I just did what I was paid to do.

753
00:50:04,401 --> 00:50:06,101
Unlock it.

754
00:50:27,353 --> 00:50:29,145
- Please let me see it.
- You can't.

755
00:50:29,145 --> 00:50:30,505
Bo Na, you're here?

756
00:50:30,505 --> 00:50:32,649
The kids wanted some, so we came.

757
00:50:32,649 --> 00:50:34,129
And while I was paying for a second...

758
00:50:34,129 --> 00:50:35,312
I asked to see the CCTV inside,

759
00:50:35,312 --> 00:50:36,657
[Authorized Personnel Only]
but they said no.

760
00:50:36,657 --> 00:50:40,289
Well, I told you I can't
just show it to anyone.

761
00:50:40,289 --> 00:50:42,933
If it's that important, bring the police.

762
00:50:42,933 --> 00:50:44,441
Excuse me.

763
00:50:44,441 --> 00:50:46,141
Hey!

764
00:50:51,381 --> 00:50:53,165
Oh, my. Who is that woman?

765
00:50:53,165 --> 00:50:55,978
Bo Na, do you know her?

766
00:51:09,057 --> 00:51:14,697
<i>Lately, I sometimes sense
something strange around me.</i>

767
00:51:14,697 --> 00:51:20,412
<i>Every time, every cell in
my body goes on high alert.</i>

768
00:51:21,253 --> 00:51:24,297
<i>I get this feeling that some danger</i>

769
00:51:24,297 --> 00:51:28,278
<i>stemming from me
could reach my child, my husband,</i>

770
00:51:29,049 --> 00:51:31,425
my family...

771
00:51:31,425 --> 00:51:33,145
Anxiety.

772
00:51:36,869 --> 00:51:41,212
<i>And every time, I pray with all my heart.</i>

773
00:51:42,169 --> 00:51:44,412
<i>If the blade cannot be stopped,</i>

774
00:51:45,049 --> 00:51:47,317
<i>let it come to me.</i>

775
00:51:47,317 --> 00:51:51,213
<i>Let the gun aim only at me.</i>

776
00:51:51,213 --> 00:51:52,913
Yul!

777
00:52:03,953 --> 00:52:05,812
Oh, Yul!

778
00:52:17,913 --> 00:52:19,165
Kwon Yul!

779
00:52:19,165 --> 00:52:20,469
Huh? Mommy!

780
00:52:20,469 --> 00:52:22,573
Lady, my mommy is here!

781
00:52:22,573 --> 00:52:24,581
Huh?

782
00:52:24,581 --> 00:52:26,569
Where did she go?

783
00:52:26,569 --> 00:52:28,177
Who?

784
00:52:28,177 --> 00:52:29,373
Yul, who was here?

785
00:52:29,373 --> 00:52:31,565
- Huh?
- Yeah, your friend.

786
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:32,693
My friend?

787
00:52:32,693 --> 00:52:35,789
Yeah. She was pushing me
on the swing just now.

788
00:52:35,789 --> 00:52:37,745
But where did she go?

789
00:52:47,797 --> 00:52:51,945
Yul, I told you not
to follow strangers, remember?

790
00:52:51,945 --> 00:52:54,897
How could you come here alone
without telling Ms. Hee Seon?

791
00:52:54,897 --> 00:52:57,769
She's not a stranger. She's your friend.

792
00:52:57,769 --> 00:52:59,778
How do you know she's my friend?

793
00:52:59,778 --> 00:53:01,909
I've never shown you my friends.

794
00:53:01,909 --> 00:53:04,489
She showed me a photo of you two.

795
00:53:04,489 --> 00:53:06,189
A picture?

796
00:53:07,669 --> 00:53:09,712
Mommy, see? It's her.

797
00:53:14,065 --> 00:53:18,761
<i>"The vital spot of every beast is the eye."</i>

798
00:53:18,761 --> 00:53:20,681
<i>How is it? Pretty awesome, right?</i>

799
00:53:20,681 --> 00:53:24,833
<i>Enough playing around. Hurry over.</i>

800
00:53:24,833 --> 00:53:26,612
<i>I miss you.</i>

801
00:53:27,969 --> 00:53:30,221
As I mentioned on the phone,

802
00:53:30,221 --> 00:53:35,453
he was a teacher who was
respected his whole life.

803
00:53:35,453 --> 00:53:36,605
- I see.
- Yeah.

804
00:53:36,605 --> 00:53:41,485
Even now, his former students
still visit him on Teachers' Day.

805
00:53:46,861 --> 00:53:52,337
That was taken when he went to
Cambodia last summer.

806
00:53:52,337 --> 00:53:53,769
Cambodia?

807
00:53:53,769 --> 00:53:55,452
That's Angkor Wat in the background.

808
00:53:55,452 --> 00:53:58,649
It was one of his bucket-list trips.

809
00:53:58,649 --> 00:54:04,518
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

810
00:54:10,209 --> 00:54:11,909
Hello.

811
00:54:13,385 --> 00:54:16,918
You remember me, right?
We met at the restaurant the other day.

812
00:54:17,733 --> 00:54:19,118
Oh, yes.

813
00:54:19,118 --> 00:54:24,085
It's just that you seemed to
have something to tell me that day.

814
00:54:24,085 --> 00:54:27,985
Could you tell me now, if that's okay?

815
00:54:35,452 --> 00:54:38,057
They came to the restaurant together.
Both of them.

816
00:54:38,057 --> 00:54:43,213
By both, you mean the doctor and...

817
00:54:43,213 --> 00:54:46,318
The middle school teacher who was shot first.

818
00:54:54,689 --> 00:54:56,941
Not just long-range.
Get me something for close range too.

819
00:54:56,941 --> 00:54:58,921
A suppressor, a knife, and a flashlight too.

820
00:54:58,921 --> 00:55:00,577
Hurry.

821
00:55:00,577 --> 00:55:02,645
Found it!

822
00:55:02,645 --> 00:55:06,773
The vehicle is currently
at the Yanghwa Han River Park parking lot.

823
00:55:06,773 --> 00:55:09,045
Finally!

824
00:55:09,045 --> 00:55:10,653
Get ready to move out.

825
00:55:10,653 --> 00:55:12,353
Yes, sir!

826
00:55:18,573 --> 00:55:20,629
Huh? Yul, Daddy's home!

827
00:55:20,629 --> 00:55:22,885
- I'm home.
- Daddy!

828
00:55:22,885 --> 00:55:25,318
Yul! There you are!

829
00:55:25,318 --> 00:55:26,621
You're home?

830
00:55:26,621 --> 00:55:28,549
What brings you here? Where is Bo Na?

831
00:55:28,549 --> 00:55:32,321
She had something urgent come up,
so she asked me to watch Yul.

832
00:55:32,321 --> 00:55:33,361
Something urgent? What happened?

833
00:55:33,361 --> 00:55:37,018
Well, I don't know either.
Must be something at work.

834
00:56:23,285 --> 00:56:25,485
Hi, my friend.

835
00:56:27,617 --> 00:56:29,145
Oh...

836
00:56:29,145 --> 00:56:32,133
Should I greet you the Korean way here?

837
00:56:32,133 --> 00:56:35,009
It's been a while, Yoo Bo Na.

838
00:56:35,009 --> 00:56:37,165
Why did you kill those people?

839
00:56:37,165 --> 00:56:39,093
What?

840
00:56:39,093 --> 00:56:42,665
That's the first thing you ask
before we've even caught up?

841
00:56:42,665 --> 00:56:46,985
Because I need to decide whether to kill you.

842
00:56:48,085 --> 00:56:49,653
Right.

843
00:56:49,653 --> 00:56:52,089
Our noble Kingfisher

844
00:56:52,089 --> 00:56:55,917
isn't the type to kill just anyone
over a bad mood.

845
00:56:55,917 --> 00:56:57,818
Should I wait longer?

846
00:56:58,485 --> 00:57:00,681
Sorry to disappoint you.

847
00:57:00,681 --> 00:57:03,118
That won't be enough to kill me.

848
00:57:05,753 --> 00:57:09,552
Did you know grilled bananas
taste like roasted sweet potatoes?

849
00:57:12,069 --> 00:57:14,441
There was a woman who always asked

850
00:57:14,441 --> 00:57:18,105
if I'd eaten whenever I came back from a job.

851
00:57:18,105 --> 00:57:20,833
She was a woman selling
cheap food on the street.

852
00:57:20,833 --> 00:57:23,852
No matter how often I ignored her,
she'd ask every day.

853
00:57:25,573 --> 00:57:27,552
"Have you eaten?"

854
00:57:28,217 --> 00:57:30,533
She wasn't afraid of anything.

855
00:57:30,533 --> 00:57:33,585
To someone who'd just
come back from killing someone...

856
00:57:35,133 --> 00:57:39,552
One day, I was hungry,
so I stopped and looked.

857
00:57:39,552 --> 00:57:43,985
She gathered up some food
and had her little daughter bring it to me.

858
00:57:45,437 --> 00:57:50,577
From then on, grilled bananas
from that woman became my dinner.

859
00:57:50,577 --> 00:57:52,718
One day, the mom and daughter

860
00:57:53,501 --> 00:57:57,077
were found dead in a pile of trash.

861
00:57:57,077 --> 00:58:01,518
It took me a while to find out who did it.

862
00:58:03,025 --> 00:58:06,152
I wondered whether to gouge out their eyes

863
00:58:06,152 --> 00:58:08,518
or tear them apart.

864
00:58:09,518 --> 00:58:14,053
While having fun pondering that,
I thought this way was pretty good too.

865
00:58:14,053 --> 00:58:18,385
Kill the ones who deserve it
and bring down Kingfisher too.

866
00:58:19,657 --> 00:58:21,357
Bang!

867
00:58:22,909 --> 00:58:25,725
Why are you doing this to me?

868
00:58:25,725 --> 00:58:28,629
I don't think I've done anything to you.

869
00:58:28,629 --> 00:58:30,352
Because you annoy me.

870
00:58:31,701 --> 00:58:35,452
Seeing you living like that
while I live like this,

871
00:58:36,245 --> 00:58:38,318
it makes my stomach churn.

872
00:58:42,418 --> 00:58:47,081
I killed that girl to protect Yoo Bo Na.

873
00:58:47,081 --> 00:58:51,318
I thought that's what you wanted,
Mama. Was I wrong?

874
00:58:52,113 --> 00:58:54,765
You should've killed Yoo Bo Na instead.

875
00:58:54,765 --> 00:58:56,465
What do you mean...

876
00:58:59,252 --> 00:59:04,597
Yoo Bo Na said,
"You should've killed me instead."

877
00:59:04,597 --> 00:59:06,385
Do you understand what that means?

878
00:59:08,613 --> 00:59:11,452
Not really.

879
00:59:12,637 --> 00:59:16,533
You don't know what Yoo Bo Na knows.

880
00:59:16,533 --> 00:59:18,701
That's why.

881
00:59:18,701 --> 00:59:20,485
That's why I'm casting you out.

882
00:59:20,485 --> 00:59:23,541
You're... kicking me out?

883
00:59:23,541 --> 00:59:24,897
Why?

884
00:59:24,897 --> 00:59:26,537
I... I...

885
00:59:26,537 --> 00:59:29,718
A girl who could kill without batting an eye.

886
00:59:29,718 --> 00:59:31,797
I was worried, but I kept watching.

887
00:59:31,797 --> 00:59:35,352
Sometimes, that nature
can be useful in the field.

888
00:59:35,352 --> 00:59:40,821
But you shouldn't have crossed the line.

889
00:59:40,821 --> 00:59:44,785
You shouldn't have proven
what kind of person you are.

890
00:59:44,785 --> 00:59:48,718
I wanted to be family.

891
00:59:49,957 --> 00:59:55,752
But no matter how hard I tried,
you only looked at Bo Na.

892
00:59:56,413 --> 00:59:58,673
How are we so different?

893
00:59:58,673 --> 01:00:00,885
She kills people, and so do I!

894
01:00:00,885 --> 01:00:02,969
It's just a fine line.

895
01:00:02,969 --> 01:00:05,269
Separated by a single fine line.

896
01:00:05,269 --> 01:00:10,113
How big a difference
that fine line makes will be proven

897
01:00:10,113 --> 01:00:13,552
by how your lives turn out.

898
01:00:14,273 --> 01:00:16,052
Don't you agree?

899
01:00:16,853 --> 01:00:20,649
<i>I should have killed you back then
instead of that girl.</i>

900
01:00:20,649 --> 01:00:24,877
That's how I was abandoned,
and this is how I live now.

901
01:00:24,877 --> 01:00:26,577
Thanks to you.

902
01:00:28,349 --> 01:00:30,049
No.

903
01:00:31,273 --> 01:00:34,318
You're the one who made you who you are.

904
01:00:36,205 --> 01:00:38,933
If you got what you wanted,
now go home quietly.

905
01:00:38,933 --> 01:00:40,969
While you're still alive.

906
01:00:40,969 --> 01:00:43,152
It's too late for that.

907
01:00:43,849 --> 01:00:47,752
I figured you'd be living
more or less like me.

908
01:00:48,397 --> 01:00:50,889
- <i>But...</i>
- Kingfisher,

909
01:00:50,889 --> 01:00:52,745
isn't he honestly amazing?

910
01:00:52,745 --> 01:00:54,109
He really is!

911
01:00:54,109 --> 01:00:55,909
The world needs someone like that.

912
01:00:55,909 --> 01:00:59,117
I wonder what he's like. I'm so curious.

913
01:00:59,117 --> 01:01:00,789
I'd love to meet him.

914
01:01:00,789 --> 01:01:04,417
<i>People here revere you like a hero?</i>

915
01:01:04,417 --> 01:01:08,652
While over there, everyone treats me
like a criminal punk.

916
01:01:10,221 --> 01:01:11,985
Mommy, are we staying the night?

917
01:01:11,985 --> 01:01:13,718
Yeah, we're staying one night.

918
01:01:13,718 --> 01:01:14,752
Yay!

919
01:01:14,752 --> 01:01:18,518
<i>You've got a loving husband,
a beautiful daughter, and...</i>

920
01:01:19,761 --> 01:01:21,921
<i>you even have a family.</i>

921
01:01:21,921 --> 01:01:24,652
<i>You even look pretty happy.</i>

922
01:01:31,033 --> 01:01:32,952
It's not fair.

923
01:01:34,457 --> 01:01:35,881
What we do...

924
01:01:35,881 --> 01:01:38,205
isn't all that different.

925
01:01:38,205 --> 01:01:39,905
You and I

926
01:01:40,737 --> 01:01:43,337
are going to hell when we die.

927
01:01:43,337 --> 01:01:45,718
The same hell?

928
01:01:46,509 --> 01:01:47,869
That sounds somewhat fair.

929
01:01:47,869 --> 01:01:50,152
I'll take my fair share of punishment.

930
01:01:50,941 --> 01:01:53,821
If there's punishment
I have to face while I'm alive,

931
01:01:53,821 --> 01:01:55,585
I'll take that too.

932
01:01:56,401 --> 01:01:58,101
But...

933
01:01:59,369 --> 01:02:01,152
leave my family out of this.

934
01:02:02,145 --> 01:02:04,285
I'm warning you.

935
01:02:04,285 --> 01:02:08,869
If you lay a finger on
my husband or my child,

936
01:02:08,869 --> 01:02:11,653
I'll make you experience hell
while you're still alive.

937
01:02:11,653 --> 01:02:13,737
Is that so?

938
01:02:13,737 --> 01:02:16,485
Then you can experience hell
while you're alive too.

939
01:02:17,745 --> 01:02:21,121
Get destroyed just like me.

940
01:02:21,121 --> 01:02:23,818
Forget everything you hold dear.

941
01:03:40,661 --> 01:03:44,772
[A Bona Fide Killer]

942
01:03:44,796 --> 01:03:47,533
Try killing me in front of your husband.

943
01:03:47,533 --> 01:03:49,352
It's you, Layla.

944
01:03:49,352 --> 01:03:50,352
Let's get her.

945
01:03:50,352 --> 01:03:52,605
The suspect must be taken alive.

946
01:03:52,605 --> 01:03:56,293
Yoo Bo Na, enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.

947
01:03:56,293 --> 01:03:58,229
Dong Jin's here. We have to go.

948
01:03:58,229 --> 01:03:59,609
We have to go. Hurry.

949
01:03:59,609 --> 01:04:02,313
I'll become your living hell.

950
01:04:02,313 --> 01:04:03,365
Ceasefire!

951
01:04:03,365 --> 01:04:07,518
Without you... how am I supposed to live?

952
01:04:09,329 --> 01:04:10,007
[Mommy, I miss you. I love you so much]
